    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "THE SATURDAY EVENING POST\nAugust 24, 1946\nORLD AIRWAIS\nPAA\nFlight-time Nears for a \"Pan-Am\" Flagship Bound Out for Europe\nThe best of TRAVELINg... with the best of CoMPANIONS\nBERMUDA\nSanta\nVACATION TIME! And time to wish\n\"Bon Voyage and happy landing!\" to\nfriends. One grand way to say it is with a Whitman's Sampler. Whether\ntraveling by air or land or sea, it brings smiles to the miles. For America's\nbest-liked chocolates are truly good companions-always.\nP. S. And take along a Whitman's Sampler when you go visiting-to add to\nyour welcome! It's the thoughtful thing to do.\n•МЕЖІС\nBARX\nINCH\ncOOL... COOL... The wonderful smooth, clean\ntaste of Whitman peppermint... pure, fine pepper-\nmint, exclusively Whitman's these past 35 years\n... blended into a mellow cream and covered, like\nother Sampler delights, in matchless Whitman\nchocolate. Sampling's fun!\nhelman's\nSampler\nHOCOLATES \u0026 CONFECTIONS.\nCopr. 1946, Stephen F. Whitman \u0026 Son, Inc., Phila.\nA\nW\nOMAN\nNEVER\nROCKIES\nWhitman's\nCHOCOLATES\nFORGETS THE MAN WHO REMEMBERS"
